    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460-a1">

                <pb facs="0554" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg466"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr. Mariscal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to my note of the 13th
                    instant relative to the case of H. C. Harding and H. E. Dugat, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith, for the information of your excellency, an extract from a
                    letter, under date of the 19th instant, which I have just received from the
                    American consul at Matamoros. The consul’s allusion to the fact that the guard,
                    Arguelles, is a nephew of the governor has no weight in the matter, according to
                    my opinion, as I do not believe that the governor would be influenced by that
                    fact in the performance of any of his official duties.</p>
                <p>I hope that your excellency may soon be able to inform me that the case against
                    these American citizens has been judicially determined, or dismissed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
